Bauify

Bauify began as the `analyzers/` subsystem proposed to Archify in
https://github.com/tt-a1i/archify/pull/352. At the Archify maintainer's
suggestion it now lives as an independent tool that produces Archify's
diagram IR rather than living inside Archify.

The Git history of this repository was split from that pull request with
`git subtree split` and preserves the original commits and authorship,
including fixes contributed by tt-a1i (Archify's author):

  - fix(analyzers): preserve import facts and cover extraction regressions
  - fix(analyzers): constrain createRequire to the source module base

Archify itself (https://github.com/tt-a1i/archify) is MIT-licensed and is
not bundled here; Bauify invokes a separately installed Archify CLI.
